# Video Production Format

## What this skill does, and what it does not

The **youtube-script** skill decides *what the video says*. This skill decides *how that finished script is packaged* so every voiceover, image, animation, sound effect and text card can be generated independently and dropped into the editor without guesswork.

This skill **never** changes the story, the facts, the jokes or the wording. The only edits allowed to spoken text are the VibeVoice text normalizations listed under *VO text rules*. If the script breaks a production limit (too many voices, a scene nothing can show), stop and send it back to the script step with the reason. Do not quietly rewrite it.

Every rule below marked **MUST** or **NEVER** is a hard rule. A package that breaks one is not finished.

---

## 1. The package

For each video, create exactly this tree. Folder and file names are fixed.

```text
V###-<video-slug>/
├── 00_brief/
│   └── brief.md
├── 01_script/
│   ├── script.md
│   ├── vo_index.md
│   └── vo/
│       ├── VO-001.txt
│       ├── VO-002.txt
│       └── ...
├── 02_voice_design/
│   └── characters.md
├── 03_moodboard/
│   └── moodboard.md
├── 04_images/
│   ├── images.md
│   └── thumbnail.md
├── 05_animations/
│   └── animations.md
├── 06_sfx/
│   └── sfx.md
└── 07_timeline/
    └── timeline.csv
```

- `V###` is the channel's video number (`V001`), `<video-slug>` is lowercase-hyphenated (`V001-still-scared-of-things`).
- No other top-level folders. No empty files: if a video truly has no dialogue characters, `characters.md` contains one line: `No character voices in this video.`
- One script per video. No A/B variations.

### Generated asset filenames

The user's generated files MUST use the asset ID as the filename, so the editor import matches the timeline:

| Asset | ID | File the user saves |
|---|---|---|
| Voiceover block | `VO-001` | `VO-001.wav` |
| Image | `IMG-001` | `IMG-001.png` |
| Animation | `ANM-001` | `ANM-001.mp4` |
| Sound effect | `SFX-001` | `SFX-001.wav` |
| Ambience bed | `AMB-001` | `AMB-001.wav` |
| Music (only if asked) | `MUS-001` | `MUS-001.wav` |
| Character voice reference | `ANCESTOR_1` | `ANCESTOR_1.wav` |
| Moodboard sheet | `MB-CHAR-01` etc. | `MB-CHAR-01.png` |

