## 2. IDs

| Thing | Format | Example |
|---|---|---|
| Segment | `SEG-##` | `SEG-00` (cold open), `SEG-01` |
| Spoken line | `L###` | `L001` |
| Hold (intentional silence) | `H###` | `H001` |
| VO block | `VO-###` | `VO-004` |
| Still image | `IMG-###` | `IMG-017` |
| Animation | `ANM-###` | `ANM-006` |
| SFX event | `SFX-###` | `SFX-003` |
| Ambience bed | `AMB-###` | `AMB-001` |
| On-screen text | `TXT-###` | `TXT-005` |
| Speaker | `NARRATOR`, or UPPER_SNAKE name | `ANCESTOR_1` |
| Moodboard entry | `MB-<TYPE>-##` | `MB-CHAR-01`, `MB-ENV-02`, `MB-PROP-03`, `MB-DEV-01` |

Rules:
- Three-digit zero padding. Numbered in timeline order.
- **NEVER** reuse or renumber an ID once the package is delivered, because generated files are already named after it. When a re-time splits an asset, add a letter suffix (`IMG-045b`); when an asset is dropped, retire its ID and leave the gap.
- Speaker names are identities, never moods: `ANCESTOR_1`, not `SCARED_ANCESTOR`.

