## 15. Workflow

1. Receive the finished script, its verify list and uncertainty note from the youtube-script step. Do not start from a draft.
2. Fill `brief.md` header fields: title, target, WPM, format.
3. Split the script into `L###` lines (Section 5 rules) and add holds.
4. Group lines into VO blocks, write `vo/VO-###.txt` with the normalization rules, and fill `vo_index.md`.
5. Compute estimated timings for every line and the segment map.
6. Write `characters.md` for every non-narrator speaker.
7. Write `moodboard.md` for every character, environment, prop and device the video needs.
8. Plan the shot list line by line: which visual starts where (anchors), still or animation, keeping to the limits in Section 8.
9. Write `images.md`, `thumbnail.md` and `animations.md`.
10. Write `sfx.md` and the text cards.
11. Build `timeline.csv`, then compute the counts and percentages for `brief.md`.
12. Run the validation below. Fix and re-run until everything passes.
13. Deliver the package. When the user later gives VO timings, run the re-time procedure (Section 3) and deliver `v2-retimed`.

