## 16. Validation (every item MUST pass)

**Structure**
- [ ] Exact folder tree and filenames from Section 1; nothing extra, nothing empty.
- [ ] One script, no variations.
- [ ] Every ID is unique, correctly formatted and in timeline order.

**Script and VO**
- [ ] Every narrator line is one sentence; every dialogue line is one turn.
- [ ] Every line has TIME, SPEAKER, VO, TEXT, VISUALS, SFX and TXT fields.
- [ ] Every line belongs to exactly one VO block; blocks are ≤ 200 words; ≤ 4 speakers per block; ≤ 3 designed character voices in the video.
- [ ] VO files contain only speakable text: no IDs, notes, tags, parentheses, `[pause]`, symbols, digits or disallowed punctuation.
- [ ] No block starts with "Welcome", "Hello", "Hi" or "However".
- [ ] Every respelling is logged in `vo_index.md`.

**Voices**
- [ ] No narrator entry in `characters.md`.
- [ ] Every non-narrator speaker has an entry with prompt (50–110 words), reference script (55–85 words, not from the video) and contrast note.
- [ ] No real-person or celebrity references.

**Visuals**
- [ ] V1 has no gaps or overlaps from `00:00:00.000` to the last line's end.
- [ ] Every still shown 0.6 s ≤ d < 2.0 s. Every animation 2.0 s ≤ d < 10.0 s.
- [ ] Animation share of screen time is 45–55 %.
- [ ] Every animation names an existing source image.
- [ ] Every prompt is free of style/medium words, text, logos and negations inside the prompt.
- [ ] Every shot's characters, environments and props exist in the moodboard, with canonical descriptions pasted in verbatim.
- [ ] Ancestor-as-shadow device appears in the video.
- [ ] Nothing graphic; nothing that reads as children's content.
- [ ] Every thumbnail element appears in the video, and the title's question is answered.

**Sound and text**
- [ ] Every SFX prompt starts with `TrackType: SFX.`, has source, action and recording, and a generate duration.
- [ ] No music unless the user asked.
- [ ] Text cards start every 15–30 s, 2–5 words, 1.5–4.0 s each.

**Timing**
- [ ] Every timestamp is `HH:MM:SS.mmm`; every `end` = `start` + `duration`.
- [ ] Every visual, SFX and text card has an anchor that points to an existing line or hold and cue word.
- [ ] Estimated runtime is within ±10 % of the target.
- [ ] Cold open ends by 00:00:30; the first named evidence starts by 00:02:00.
- [ ] `brief.md` counts match `timeline.csv`.

Report the validation result at the end of delivery as a short pass list. If anything had to be sent back to the script step, say what and why.
